<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scania is the southernmost province of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">Øresund</a> strait. Long part of Denmark, it was ceded to Sweden by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> in 1658. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> note that Danish forces invaded Scania after Sweden's defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a>, though it remained Swedish.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scania.jpg" alt="Scania" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jorchr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Willows_and_flowering_rapefield.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
